@page "/colors"

<PageTitle>Colors</PageTitle>

<h3>Colors</h3>
<p>
    All charts need to be colored, from the slices of a pie or donut chart
    to the bars of a histogram, and even the series of a line chart.<br />
    <b>Color palettes</b> originated as a convenient way to assign a set of colors to chart data,
    ensuring the colors are clearly distinguishable from one another while maintaining a consistent tone. <br />
    There are two types of available palettes, those with a preset color set and those that are random.
    <div class="card overflow-hidden">
        <div class="card-body overflow-auto">
            <table class="table text-nowrap align-middle mb-0 border">
                <tr>
                    <th>Type</th>
                    <th>.ctor</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="token class-name font-monospace">CyclicPalette</span></td>
                    <td class="font-monospace"><span class="token keyword">Color</span>[]</td>
                    <td>Configurable palette with a selected set of colors that cycle continuously</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="token class-name font-monospace">RandomPalette</span></td>
                    <td class="font-monospace"><span class="token property">Int32</span></td>
                    <td>Random color palette configurable with a seed, that determines the sequence</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
</p>
<p>
    Both types of palettes implement the same interface <span class="token keyword font-monospace">IColorStream</span>:
    <div class="card overflow-hidden">
        <div class="card-body overflow-auto">
            <table class="table text-nowrap align-middle mb-0 border">
                <tr>
                    <th>Method</th>
                    <th>Output</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="token function-name font-monospace">Next</span></td>
                    <td class="font-monospace"><span class="token keyword">Color</span></td>
                    <td>Next color taken from the set configured in the constructor</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="token function-name font-monospace">Reset</span></td>
                    <td class="font-monospace"><span class="token property">void</span></td>
                    <td>Reset the palette to the beginning.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
</p>
<p>
    There are already four preset palettes with the following colors:
</p>
<div class="row row-cols-md-4 row-cols-2 g-4">
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h6 class="text-center font-monospace"><span class="token keyword">Palettes</span>.Primary</h6>
                <div class="border"><Palette Colors="Palettes.Primary" Size="8"></Palette></div>
            </div>
        </div>                  
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h6 class="text-center font-monospace"><span class="token keyword">Palettes</span>.Pastel</h6>
                <div class="border"><Palette Colors="Palettes.Pastel" Size="8"></Palette></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h6 class="text-center font-monospace"><span class="token keyword">Palettes</span>.Light</h6>
                <div class="border"><Palette Colors="Palettes.Light" Size="8"></Palette></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card overflow-hidden">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h6 class="text-center font-monospace"><span class="token keyword">Palettes</span>.Dark</h6>
                <div class="border"><Palette Colors="Palettes.Dark" Size="8"></Palette></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
